## 2. Judgment calls (all also in module docs)

- **Key shape:** channel as `u8` (not `ChannelKind` — keeps surface disjoint from umber-core; exhaustive match fails loud on a future third kind); tile stays `TileId` grid cells, **not** `u16` (pool addresses UV-grid output of `tile_for`, not UDIM ids; conflating them mis-addresses multi-tile sets).
- **Iterative per-layer dispatches** instead of single-pass `binding_array`: only proven binding shapes (paint.rs), no max-layers cap; identical per-texel math.
- **Coverage-gated kernel** (`out = dst + (blend−dst)·src_a·opacity`): naive per-channel fold lets transparent `Normal` erase the stack; gating is bit-identical to `composite_channel` for opaque sources (pinned by test) and a no-op for transparent ones.
- **Alpha = straight-alpha over**, not a 4th `blend_channel` (Multiply-on-alpha keeps opaque-over-translucent translucent — wrong).
- **Folders/`Passthrough`/missing tiles = transparent no-ops** (membership not modeled in umber-core yet); non-passthrough folder isolation deferred, recorded in docs.
- **Memory v1:** 1 MiB/tile, 64 MiB per full 4K layer-channel, 3.2 GiB for 10×5×4K (past the ~2 GiB §12 CPU-journal budget — a separate pool — and reference-GPU class in `docs/perf/protocol.md`); manual eviction retained (auto-LRU would break the pinned contract and needs Wave-3 readback), cap advisory only.
- **GPU-vs-CPU ±1 LSB** with reason (UNORM rounding, FMA); exact pins live on the CPU side. Unknown WGSL mode ids fall back to Normal.

